                       1.Brute Force
class Solution {
    public boolean containsNearbyDuplicate(int[] nums, int k) {
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            for (int j = i + 1; j <= i + k && j < nums.length; j++) {
                if (nums[i] == nums[j]) {
                    return true;
                }
            }
        }
        return false;
    }
}
                  2.Intuition
We only need to know whether the current element has appeared in the last k indices.
Maintain a sliding window of size at most k using a HashSet.
If the current element is already in the set, a duplicate exists within distance k, so return true.
Otherwise, add the current element to the set.
If the window size exceeds k, remove the element that is now outside the window (nums[i - k]).
           
                  3.Time Complexity
Time Complexity: O(n)
